Is this what it means?

278
00:17:55,968 --> 00:17:56,968
To not run away?

279
00:17:57,968 --> 00:17:59,968
I wanted to have memories of not running away

280
00:18:00,968 --> 00:18:01,968
No more running

281
00:18:02,968 --> 00:18:05,968
What if I was just pretending not to run away this whole time?

282
00:18:10,968 --> 00:18:11,968
Then what do I do?

283
00:18:12,968 --> 00:18:14,968
Who the hell even knows anymore?

284
00:18:15,968 --> 00:18:16,968
Something's different

285
00:18:17,968 --> 00:18:20,968
I'm not the kind of student I imagined I'd be

286
00:18:20,968 --> 00:18:26,968
I thought I'd be able to handle all of this responsibility

287
00:18:27,968 --> 00:18:28,968
It sounds amazing

288
00:18:31,968 --> 00:18:33,968
I thought if I left home

289
00:18:34,968 --> 00:18:35,968
That I would be able to pay the rent

290
00:18:36,968 --> 00:18:38,968
And figure out a way to feed myself

291
00:18:39,968 --> 00:18:41,968
That I would be considered an adult

292
00:18:44,968 --> 00:18:46,968
And as an adult

293
00:18:46,968 --> 00:18:47,968
As an adult

294
00:18:52,968 --> 00:18:53,968
I thought

295
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:55,968
I wouldn't have to cry

296
00:18:56,968 --> 00:18:57,968
Anymore

297
00:19:01,968 --> 00:19:02,968
Hey, Kiriyama?

298
00:19:03,968 --> 00:19:04,968
What's wrong with you?

299
00:19:04,968 --> 00:19:05,968
Why are you crying?

300
00:19:06,968 --> 00:19:07,968
What the hell is this?

301
00:19:07,968 --> 00:19:08,968
A job magazine?

302
00:19:10,968 --> 00:19:11,968
I don't get it

303
00:19:12,968 --> 00:19:14,968
Why is the student sitting on the stairs all alone

304
00:19:14,968 --> 00:19:16,968
Crying over a job magazine?

305
00:19:17,968 --> 00:19:19,968
There's something messed up about this whole situation

306
00:19:20,968 --> 00:19:21,968
It's not right!

307
00:19:21,968 --> 00:19:24,968
Besides, he's the fifth middle school student to ever become a pro shogi player

308
00:19:25,968 --> 00:19:27,968
He's the rising star of the shogi world

309
00:19:28,968 --> 00:19:29,968
There's so much to dig into here

310
00:19:29,968 --> 00:19:30,968
I don't know where to start

311
00:19:31,968 --> 00:19:35,968
Here, have this

312
00:19:36,968 --> 00:19:37,968
But I...

313
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:38,968
Never mind, just eat it

314
00:19:39,968 --> 00:19:41,968
Who wants to have a cold lunch when they're totally depressed?

315
00:19:42,968 --> 00:19:43,968
That stuff will kill you

316
00:19:44,968 --> 00:19:45,968
But this will warm you up

317
00:19:46,968 --> 00:19:49,968
Go on, otherwise you'll lose half your hit points

318
00:19:54,968 --> 00:19:55,968
So, Kiriyama

319
00:19:56,968 --> 00:19:57,968
I've been thinking

320
00:19:58,968 --> 00:19:59,968
Why don't you move back to your mentor's house?

321
00:20:00,968 --> 00:20:01,968
Uh...

322
00:20:02,968 --> 00:20:03,968
But... I...

323
00:20:04,968 --> 00:20:07,968
You've got all these matches and rank-deciding competitions to worry about

324
00:20:08,968 --> 00:20:10,968
There are tests to study for in high school and meals to make

325
00:20:11,968 --> 00:20:12,968
You have laundry to do

326
00:20:13,968 --> 00:20:15,968
And you have to deal with whatever else is going on in your life

327
00:20:16,968 --> 00:20:17,968
That's a lot

328
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:20,968
More than enough for a 17-year-old to handle

329
00:20:21,968 --> 00:20:22,968
Yeah, but...

330
00:20:22,968 --> 00:20:24,968
Face it, it's too much to deal with all by yourself

331
00:20:25,968 --> 00:20:26,968
Hmm...

332
00:20:30,968 --> 00:20:32,968
It's too bad about the Shishio tournament

333
00:20:33,968 --> 00:20:34,968
Saw it online

334
00:20:35,968 --> 00:20:37,968
Shimada Eighth Den

335
00:20:38,968 --> 00:20:39,968
He's one hell of a good player

336
00:20:40,968 --> 00:20:42,968
He came on the scene with Grandmaster Soya

337
00:20:43,968 --> 00:20:44,968
But never managed to stand out

338
00:20:45,968 --> 00:20:48,968
He was even able to make it all the way to A-Class before long

339
00:20:49,968 --> 00:20:51,968
He's proven to be the epitome of ambition

340
00:20:51,968 --> 00:20:53,968
And recently...

341
00:20:54,968 --> 00:20:56,968
He's been a regular at all the title matches

342
00:20:57,968 --> 00:20:58,968
Incredible, huh?

343
00:21:01,968 --> 00:21:02,968
Why do you know so much?

344
00:21:03,968 --> 00:21:04,968
We're both the same age

345
00:21:05,968 --> 00:21:06,968
So I'm curious

346
00:21:07,968 --> 00:21:08,968
I've heard that...

347
00:21:09,968 --> 00:21:11,968
Shimada's really passionate about popularizing Shogi

348
00:21:12,968 --> 00:21:15,968
He even has a special workshop he holds where young players can train with him

349
00:21:16,968 --> 00:21:17,968
What do you think, Rei?

350
00:21:17,968 --> 00:21:19,968
Have you ever thought about something like that?

351
00:21:20,968 --> 00:21:21,968
Joining a workshop?

352
00:21:22,968 --> 00:21:23,968
Well...

353
00:21:24,968 --> 00:21:25,968
No...

354
00:21:25,968 --> 00:21:26,968
I don't know if that's really for me

355
00:21:27,968 --> 00:21:28,968
I think you should try it

356
00:21:34,968 --> 00:21:35,968
Yeah, but the thing is...

357
00:21:36,968 --> 00:21:38,968
I think Shimada's workshop is worth checking out

358
00:21:39,968 --> 00:21:43,968
I'm pretty sure that your friend Nikaido Fourth Dan is also a member there as well

359
00:21:44,968 --> 00:21:45,968
But...

360
00:21:45,968 --> 00:21:46,968
Come on, at least think about it

361
00:21:47,968 --> 00:21:50,968
Being able to learn from the person who beat you could be a huge opportunity

362
00:21:53,968 --> 00:21:54,968
Yeah, but...

363
00:21:55,968 --> 00:21:56,968
Aw, jeez!

364
00:21:57,968 --> 00:21:58,968
That's all you've been saying!

365
00:21:59,968 --> 00:22:00,968
Butt, butt, butt, butt, butt!

366
00:22:01,968 --> 00:22:03,968
If a hundred butts could open a door for you, fine!

367
00:22:04,968 --> 00:22:06,968
But stating the obvious, there ain't no door like that!

368
00:22:07,968 --> 00:22:08,968
Yeah, but...

369
00:22:08,968 --> 00:22:10,968
Don't give me any more damn butts!

370
00:22:10,968 --> 00:22:17,968
I don't get it

371
00:22:18,968 --> 00:22:21,968
Why can't we just reach out to Kiriyama and see what he says?

372
00:22:22,968 --> 00:22:25,968
Weren't you just saying something the other day about inviting him to join the workshop?

373
00:22:26,968 --> 00:22:27,968
I thought it was your idea

374
00:22:28,968 --> 00:22:29,968
Hmm...

375
00:22:30,968 --> 00:22:33,968
It's difficult to explain, but it's not for me to decide

376
00:22:33,968 --> 00:22:39,968
All we can really do right now is wait for him to come to us

377
00:22:44,968 --> 00:22:46,968
So he needs to make the first move?

378
00:22:47,968 --> 00:22:48,968
Yeah

379
00:22:51,968 --> 00:22:53,968
He needs to make the first move

380
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:34,771
Oh, Kiriyama.

381
00:24:35,171 --> 00:24:36,791
Look at this. It's amazing.

382
00:24:36,991 --> 00:24:38,151
Did they just have an argument?

383
00:24:38,491 --> 00:24:41,231
No way. I've never seen Mr. Shimada like this.

384
00:24:41,531 --> 00:24:43,871
No! That was nothing at all!

385
00:24:44,571 --> 00:24:47,191
Really? It's that embarrassing?

386
00:24:47,751 --> 00:24:50,251
What is this... feeling?

387
00:24:51,651 --> 00:24:55,011
Strawberry will be just as cute in the next March Comes In Like a Lion!

388
00:24:55,191 --> 00:24:57,071
I don't think she's in the next one.

389
00:24:57,151 --> 00:24:59,151
Why not? She's too cute not to be!

390
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:03,011
Oh, I love you!

391
00:25:03,011 --> 00:25:05,011
And don't like to do it!

392
00:25:05,851 --> 00:25:07,851
Ultimately it is when you run out of breath.

393
00:25:07,851 --> 00:25:09,931
I love you!

394
00:25:10,811 --> 00:25:12,811
Now monsieur she is your friend.

395
00:25:13,211 --> 00:25:18,171
With this belief on Strachofias on April 24.

396
00:25:18,651 --> 00:25:20,411
It signs a lie in divorce.

397
00:25:20,591 --> 00:25:22,211
On April 24.

398
00:25:22,871 --> 00:25:24,431
Let's grab a nice tie either.

399
00:25:27,191 --> 00:25:29,271
Take off one step back.

